    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter the tree-sitter dependency bump, scrolling a Ruby buffer with Tree-sitter enabled becomes very slow.\n\nThis reproduces with a small synthetic Ruby buffer containing repeated lines:\n\n```ruby\nA #\n```\n\nPressing `<C-f>` is very slow. Holding `<C-f>` makes CPU usage reach 100%.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFirst, clone `nvim-treesitter`:\n\n```sh\ngit clone --depth=1 https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter /tmp/nvim-treesitter\n```\n\nInstall the Ruby parser:\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean +'set rtp^=/tmp/nvim-treesitter' +'runtime plugin/nvim-treesitter.lua' +'TSInstall ruby'\n```\n\nWait until `:TSInstall ruby` finishes, then quit Nvim.\n\nCreate `repro.vim`:\n\n```vim\nset runtimepath^=/tmp/nvim-treesitter\nexecute 'set runtimepath^=' . fnameescape(stdpath('data') . '/site')\nruntime plugin/nvim-treesitter.lua\ncall setline(1, repeat(['A #'], 1000))\nset filetype=ruby\nset number\nset nomodified\nlua vim.treesitter.start(0, 'ruby')\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean -S repro.vim\n```\n\nAfter Nvim starts, press:\n\n```text\n<C-f>\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nPressing `<C-f>` is very slow.\n\nIf `<C-f>` is held down, CPU usage reaches 100%.\n\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nScrolling with `<C-f>` should remain responsive, and holding `<C-f>` should not cause continuous 100% CPU usage.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-881+gc040f53dc1\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nUbuntu 26.04\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ngnome-terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
