        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "The regression was indeed introduced by the changes in https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter/pull/5712. These changes were correct, but introduced a state explosion in tree-sitter's query engine. The slowdown can be fixed in ruby's queries pretty easily (and they probably should have had these anchors all along):\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/runtime/queries/ruby/highlights.scm b/runtime/queries/ruby/highlights.scm\nindex 5aa518a2..3116e06b 100644\n--- a/runtime/queries/ruby/highlights.scm\n+++ b/runtime/queries/ruby/highlights.scm\n@@ -225,20 +225,24 @@\n \n (program\n   (comment)+ @comment.documentation\n+  .\n   (class))\n \n (module\n   (comment)+ @comment.documentation\n+  .\n   (body_statement\n     (class)))\n \n (class\n   (comment)+ @comment.documentation\n+  .\n   (body_statement\n     (method)))\n \n (body_statement\n   (comment)+ @comment.documentation\n+  .\n   (method))\n \n ; Operators\n\n```\n\nThere's also a performance improvement made to the query engine in https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter/pull/5725 that should make either set of queries usable.",
